<area>: <what changed, one line>

What:
Why:
How:
Result:
Sources:
Exposure:

# Template (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Commit messages"). Lines starting with # are
# removed. Every field is required and must not be empty:
#   What:     what this commit does
#   Why:      the reason (the milestone and requirement IDs it serves)
#   How:      the approach, and anything tried and rejected
#   Result:   what the author saw when testing (the CI record is the
#             authoritative result)
#   Sources:  PROVENANCE IDs used (or "none")
#   Exposure: the author's role and exposure (e.g. "firmware side, none")
# A field may continue on the following lines, indented.
# Agent-written commits also end with these trailers:
#   Model: <exact model ID>
#   Claude-Session: <session URL>
#   Co-Authored-By: <model> <noreply@anthropic.com>
# Checked by tools/hooks/commit-msg and by CI (tools/check-commit-msg.py).
